`SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` was deprecated by Android (API 30+) and MAUI removed support for it. In .NET 10, use these approaches instead:

### 1. `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (enabled by default)

MAUI automatically scrolls focused inputs into view. If you've disabled it, re-enable it:

```csharp
// In MauiProgram.cs or per-page:
Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Connect(App.Current.Windows[0]);
```

To **disable** it on pages where you don't want it:
```csharp
Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect();
```

### 2. For a chat layout — use `AdjustPan` + layout structure

For a chat screen, structure your XAML so the input sits at the bottom of a `Grid`, and set Android to pan mode:

```xml
<!-- In your page or App.xaml.cs -->
<ContentPage xmlns:android="clr-namespace:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.PlatformConfiguration.AndroidSpecific;
    assembly=Microsoft.Maui.Controls"
    android:Application.WindowSoftInputModeAdjust="Pan">

  <Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}"
                    ItemsUpdatingScrollMode="KeepLastItemInView" />

    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" Padding="8">
      <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
      <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
  </Grid>
</ContentPage>
```

### 3. Manual inset handling (most control)

Listen for keyboard insets on Android and adjust bottom padding:

```csharp
#if ANDROID
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

// In your platform-specific setup or custom handler:
ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(
    Platform.CurrentActivity!.Window!.DecorView, 
    new KeyboardInsetsListener(bottomBar));

class KeyboardInsetsListener(View target) : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        target.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, imeInsets.Bottom);
        return insets;
    }
}
#endif
```

**TL;DR:** For a chat screen, option **2** (`AdjustPan` + `Grid` with `Auto` bottom row) is the simplest. If you need pixel-perfect control, use option **3** with IME insets.
